```javascript
// Module-scope globals, persist across parse() calls in QJSEngine
var _map  = { "OS": 0, "CPU_USAGE": 7, "CORE0": 17, ... };
var _vals = new Array(59).fill('');

function parse(frame) {
    var pairs = frame.split('|');
    for (var i = 0; i < pairs.length; i++) {
        var eq  = pairs[i].indexOf('=');
        var key = pairs[i].substring(0, eq).trim();
        var val = pairs[i].substring(eq + 1).trim();
        if (_map.hasOwnProperty(key))
            _vals[_map[key]] = val;
    }
    return _vals;
}
```

Dataset index `N` in the `.ssproj` maps to `_vals[N - 1]` (Serial Studio uses 1-based dataset indices, the JS array is 0-based).

The Control Loop runs `setup()` once when the device connects and `loop()` while it stays connected, like an Arduino sketch. Serial Studio reports the source as connected only after the saved service and notify characteristic are wired, so the script can write immediately. The handshake, condensed from the project's script:

